WEBVTT

00:00:00.185 --> 00:00:04.622
A diffusion model learns to undo a process
that turns images into noise.

00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:08.372
Each step shrinks the image a little and
adds a little Gaussian noise.

00:00:08.372 --> 00:00:12.110
After a thousand steps, almost nothing of
the image is left.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.647
Because Gaussian variances add, you do not
need to walk there.

00:00:15.647 --> 00:00:18.335
Any noise level can be reached in one
jump.

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:23.210
With zero point six four, the value two
with noise minus one becomes one.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:28.292
A network sees the noisy image and the
step, and is trained to recover the noise.

00:00:28.292 --> 00:00:30.504
Know the noise, and you have the image:

00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:32.617
rearrange the same formula.

00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:35.692
But many clean images could give the same
noisy one.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:38.767
So the best possible network outputs an
average:

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.792
the mean clean image consistent with what
it sees.

00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:44.920
Take data that is only ever plus one or
minus one,

00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:47.889
and suppose the noisy value is zero point
five.

00:00:47.888 --> 00:00:49.950
What should the best denoiser output?

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:50.675
One?

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:51.675
Something else?

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:53.238
Pause and decide.

00:00:54.671 --> 00:00:56.034
About zero point eight:

00:00:56.034 --> 00:00:59.384
a soft choice between the two examples,
never quite committing.

00:00:59.384 --> 00:01:03.009
To generate, start from pure noise and
step towards less noise.

00:01:03.009 --> 00:01:07.096
Here is a real run with the exact best
denoiser for six training images.

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:08.571
It lands on one of them.

00:01:08.571 --> 00:01:12.596
The exact denoiser can only copy, which is
why it must be learned.

00:01:12.596 --> 00:01:16.596
DDPM adds a little fresh noise at each of
a thousand steps.

00:01:16.596 --> 00:01:22.484
DDIM adds none, so one start always gives
one image, and it can skip to fifty steps.

00:01:22.846 --> 00:01:27.734
Guidance pushes past the conditional
prediction to follow a prompt more
closely.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:31.396
Weight three turns zero point five into
one point one.
